Captured public page: https://www.lapipa.io/about/people

Capture timestamp: 2026-08-05T01:11:40.126Z

Page description: Meet the minds behind LA PIPA - contributors, collaborators, and clever misfits driving innovation and creative excellence.

AboutPeopleTHEPEOPLEContributors, collaborators, clever misfits24 MINDS01Co-Founder & CreatorAlex LawtonThe creator of LA PIPA is a futurist and media expert with over 25 years of experience leading global and local media agencies. A true innovator and entrepreneur, Alex thrives on curiosity and a drive to push boundaries. His deep industry expertise and forward-thinking approach have put agencies at the forefront of the media business, making him a force in creating new opportunities in this moment of fast, Post-Digital change.★02Co-FounderDavid DeibeDr. Deibe is an expert in data processing. He earned his PhD in Information Technologies Research from the Universidade da Coruña, Spain. He has contributed significantly to the development of efficient data structures and algorithms for handling massive datasets, particularly in the visualisation and processing of point clouds. With experience in both academic research and private business, David has pioneered tools for data visualization and big data storage solutions across multiple sectors, from shipping and naval industries to marketing and media. Currently, David continues to contribute to innovative projects in data engineering and computer vision, advancing the boundaries of marketing and media data science, engineering, ML and AI, as well as providing the backbone for more sustainable advanced analytics.★03Co-FounderDory CasasThe inspiring female force among the founders, blending her deep expertise in media planning and activation, with her passion for nature, sustainability, food sovereignty, and permaculture. As a champion of these causes, Dory drives our commitment to creating conscious solutions that align with the values of our clients and the future of our planet. Her innovative mindset and dedication to regenerative practices inspire our team to incorporate sustainability into every aspect of what we do.★04Leadership & Organizational TransformationFrancesca GabettiFrancesca is a visionary leader with a deep commitment to organizational transformation, leadership development, and the promotion of conscious business practices. She leverages her expertise to help organizations enhance team performance through data-driven insights and emotional intelligence. Francesca has also played key roles in global movements like Women in Tech and Conscious Capitalism, advocating for gender diversity in technology and promoting business models that prioritize ethical leadership and social impact. Her work bridges innovation with purpose, empowering teams and organizations to thrive in an ever-evolving business landscape.★05Lead Sound DesignerEulogioHe is an artist, promoter, and entrepreneur with over 30 years in the music industry, blending his deep experience with cutting-edge sound design and music production. As the lead sound designer at LA PIPA Studios and ReMotive Media, Eulogio ensures that every audiovisual LA PIPA project features original soundscapes he and his dedicated team crafted. His passion for music production and live performance drives him to create unique audio experiences that elevate the content for brands and immersive projects. This phase of his career focuses on pushing creative boundaries while maintaining a commitment to high-quality, original sound design.★06Co-FounderJosé Luis QuirósJosé Luis is a visionary in the music industry, renowned for co-founding LA PIPA, a significant initiative aimed at revolutionizing music and cultural experiences. In addition to his innovative work with LA PIPA, he serves as the managing partner of Mestizo Producciones, where he oversees numerous projects that blend music, art, and culture. His leadership extends to directing the Gijón Sound Festival, where he curates a dynamic mix of international and local talent, further establishing his influence on the Spanish and global music scenes.★07Media & Marketing StrategistKoen SmeetsKoen Smeets is an accomplished media and marketing strategist with a wealth of global experience. He previously held the role of Global Strategy Director at Dentsu-Aegis and Starcom (London), where he honed his expertise in driving business growth and media innovation for top-tier brands. After moving to Spain, Koen led Performance Strategy across EMEA for DAC Group, further solidifying his reputation for excellence in performance-driven media. His entrepreneurial spirit ultimately led him to co-found ReMotive Media, where he continues to push boundaries in media strategy and long-term brand growth.★08Co-Founder & Open Source RingleaderRon EvansA leading figure in the open-source and IoT community. As the co-founder of LA PIPA, he plays a pivotal role in shaping the platform''s innovative direction. He is also the Open Source Ringleader, overseeing LA PIPA''s Hack Space, where he fosters a collaborative environment for creators and developers to push technological boundaries. Evans is best known for his contributions to the global IoT and robotics community. He is the creator of Gobot, a widely-used open-source framework for robotics and IoT, and GoCV, a Go-based framework for computer vision. Additionally, he is creator and maintainer of TinyGo, a compiler that brings the Go programming language to embedded systems and microcontrollers, making significant strides in IoT development. His thought leadership and technical innovations have earned him recognition at major conferences like FOSDEM and MakerFaire, and he has been instrumental in helping companies like AT&T and Intel tackle complex IoT challenges.★09Co-FounderSergio MaldonadoSergio is a data privacy expert with a proven track record in leading digital transformation. Known for his deep expertise in data management and privacy regulations, he pioneers privacy-first media solutions that drive innovation, and craft trust-driven strategies, ensuring brands navigate the evolving digital landscape ethically.★K10Co-Founder, Mestizo Producciones & LA PIPA StudiosKiko RimadaCo-Founder of Mestizo Producciones, musician, and co-creator of LA PIPA Studios, Kiko is a natural native in the Spanish independent music scene. Also known for his one of a kind band like Los Guajes, he blends cultural influences to create unique, dynamic sounds. As the co-director of the Gijón Sound Festival, Kiko has helped shape a vibrant music community, promoting both local and international talent. His passion for music production and fostering creative collaboration continues to thrive through LA PIPA Studios, a hub for content driven and streaming initiatives.★R11Founder, Ricardo Crispin & Co MotorsRicardo (Richard) CrispinRichard is a valued member of the community and the founder of Ricardo Crispin & Co Motors, a boutique operation dedicated to the curation of classic and modern classic vehicles. With a reputation built on precision, integrity, and an instinctive understanding of automotive value, Ricardo brings decades of hands-on experience to every acquisition, combining market insight with a deep appreciation for craftsmanship and design.★J12Proptech ExpertJaime PireJaime is an expert in the proptech sector, with a strong focus on integrating technology into real estate and facilities management. His expertise includes utilising digital tools and innovative solutions to streamline property management, enhance facilities operations, and improve overall efficiency. Jaime is dedicated to helping businesses adopt advanced technologies that optimize processes, making both property and facilities management more agile, cost-effective, and customer-centric.★A13VFX Artist & LA PIPA Co-CreatorAlonso VarelaAlonso is an accomplished VFX artist with an extensive portfolio that includes major films such as Ex Machina (2014), Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets (2017), Geostorm (2017), and War for the Planet of the Apes (2017), showcasing his expertise in creating visually complex and award-winning effects. His work extends to popular TV series like The Boys (2022), and many others. Beyond his long list of achievements, Alonso is an untold force behind the creation of LA PIPA, who spent many years discussing vision and ideas with Alex Lawton, of who he is a lifelong friend. At LA PIPA he focuses on collaborating towards transferring his knowledge to people in other fields, and helping young talents find their path in the global VFX industry continuing to make an impact, as a creator and also as a guide for emerging artists.★N14Business Development & Impact InvestingNacho HuiciA powerhouse in business development and impact investing, Ignacio brings sharp strategy and unstoppable energy to LA PIPA. With deep roots in sustainable energy, and open innovation, he''s driving the future through green hydrogen, storage, and solar PV projects. A natural connector with a killer network, Ignacio''s passion for startups, tech, and smart capital is matched only by his mission: building a better, more sustainable world for the next generation. Business angel, venture builder, and all-around great human being—he''s making EIT InnoEnergy''s vision a reality, and we''re very lucky to have him in our community!★B15CoordinatorBea SandeBeatriz is a star who coordinates everything at LA PIPA thanks to her ability to make complex tasks seem simple and always maintaining a positive attitude, even under heavy workloads. No matter the challenge, she consistently delivers with a smile, underscoring her commitment to a good working environment, inclusivity, tolerance, optimism and positive working relationships.★S16Creative ProfessionalSergio RedruelloSergio Redruello is a creative professional with a background in filmmaking, photography, TV, design, and digital creation. His career has spanned various fields, where he has combined his skills to engage audiences with creativity and practical solutions.★F17Surf Instructor & Mental Wellness AdvocateFernando FerraoFernando is a seasoned surf instructor who has garnered recognition through numerous surf competitions over the years. His achievements include top placements in regional and national surf events. His accolades showcase his deep connection to the ocean and his ability to navigate the challenging dynamics of competitive surfing, enhancing his credibility as a surf coach. He is also a graduate in Business administration, has a Bachelor''s degree in Marketing and management in the sports industry and is a Graduate in Psychology, allowing him to combine his love for sport with a focus on mental well-being. He is also a podcast host and radio presenter, where he shares his insights on mental health, personal development, and the surf lifestyle. A passionate supporter of lapipa.io, Fernando is committed to helping others thrive, both in the water and in their personal lives.★M18Graphic Artist & ChefMarcos GarciaMarcos Garcia is a seasoned expert in graphic art and printing, with over two decades of experience running his own studio in Northern Spain. His dedication to craftsmanship and design has made him a respected figure in the industry. Alongside his work in graphic arts, Marcos also channels his creativity into the culinary world, where his alter ego as a chef allows him to explore new forms of expression and passion. Whether in the studio or the kitchen, his attention to detail and love for his craft shine through.★P19Friend of LA PIPAPaloma RochaA great friend of LA PIPA, Paloma is going through serious problems with her back, resulting from years of hard work in the fashion industry, that make it impossible for her to do any work at all nowadays. We all hope she will be back whenever she can. Animo Paloma!★I20Artisan CandlemakerIsa RimadaIsa Rimada´s candles are a bridge to our past. Beeswax candles have been revered since ancient times- The Celts, known for their deep connection to nature and the spiritual world, often used beeswax candles in their rituals, valuing the natural, sweet scent and the bright, clean light that enhances spiritual experiences.★A21Marketing & Business StrategistArantxa AlvizArantxa is a skilled marketing and business strategist with expertise in programmatic advertising, sales management, and international expansion. She has a strong track record in driving business growth, developing go-to-market strategies, and leading client relations. With experience in both digital and cultural sectors, Arantxa excels in project management, creative innovation, and optimizing customer lifecycle marketing. Known for her strategic leadership and hands-on approach, she brings a dynamic mix of innovation and execution to every role she undertakes.★N22Academic Coordinator, Lawton SchoolNelson MendesNelson Mendes is an accomplished academic coordinator at Lawton School, cultivating a vibrant multilingual environment and ensuring high-quality language education. With a background in Modern Languages and Literatures, he leads robust educational programs and drives sustainability-focused initiatives. His strategic expertise extends to coordinating EU projects and fostering international cooperation at AACI, underscoring his commitment to innovative, inclusive learning.★G23Managing Partner, ReMotive MediaGordan DomlijaGordan is an experienced leader in the global advertising and media industry, with more than 25 years in marketing, communications, and business transformation. Based in Asia for much of his career, he has led major organizations through change and growth, combining strategic clarity with a deep understanding of people and culture. Before joining ReMotive Media as Managing Partner, Gordan served as President of Wavemaker Asia and CEO of Wavemaker China, where he helped guide the agency''s evolution across some of the region''s most dynamic markets. At ReMotive, he continues to focus on shaping the future of media and marketing—driven by curiosity, collaboration, and a commitment to meaningful, human-centered growth.★24Digital Marketing & Creative AdvertisingLuke WestlandLuke is a natural connector with over 15 years of experience in digital marketing, creative advertising, and commercial law. Known for his ability to see opportunities where others may not, Luke excels at bringing the right people together to make great things happen. With a unique mix of marketing expertise and a legal background, he has a knack for defining strategies that spark growth. Luke works closely with teams and partners to craft campaigns that not only drive results but also create genuine connections with audiences. His passion for creative, impactful advertising is matched by his commitment to ensuring everything runs smoothly and stays on track with compliance and quality standards. At heart, Luke loves seeing ideas come to life through collaboration, and his approachable, down-to-earth style makes working with him a rewarding experience.★WANT TOJOIN US?We''re always looking for clever misfits','2026-08-05T00:00:00Z') on conflict (document_id,version) do update set content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,byte_count=excluded.byte_count,extracted_text=excluded.extracted_text;
