insert into kb.document_versions (document_id,version,content_sha256,mime_type,byte_count,extracted_text,effective_from) values ((select id from kb.documents where document_id='LP-WEB-LIVE-CLUB-FOOD-DOC'),'2026-08-05-capture','4a1f47391c9a2c3f18539a61a71e8ec1947959658cbe0a43887ccdab997b0da3','text/markdown',2989,'Archive source LP-WEB-LIVE-CLUB-FOOD. Food — LA PIPA.

Captured public page: https://www.lapipa.io/club/food

Capture timestamp: 2026-08-05T01:12:07.231Z

Page description: Where permaculture meets the kitchen at LA PIPA. Growing edible gardens, fermenting tradition, and exploring food as culture, ecology, and imagination in Asturias.

ClubFoodFOODROOTSPERMACULTURE × KITCHENWhere the garden meets the tableWHAT WE BELIEVEFood is more than nourishment—it''s CULTURE, ECOLOGY, and imagination.LIVINGLARDERSOur edible landscapes grow from permaculture principles, where every plant, insect, and human plays a role in a shared ecosystem.The gardens are both classrooms and larders—places to learn, cook, and reconnect with the cycles of the earth.🌱INSPIRED BY THE WORLDRooted in the landscapes of Asturias and inspired by global examples like the Eden Project (UK) and Stone Barns Center (USA).LA PIPA integrates food, art, and sustainability into one continuous experiment.♨LA PIPAKITCHENThe heart of our community—a space for craft, learning, and sharing.Chefs, artists, farmers, and curious visitors come together to explore what happens when food becomes a creative act.FRIDAY LUNCHESOpen, communal meals celebrating what the garden and local producers bring each weekSECRET DINNERSIntimate, one-night experiences where seasonal cooking meets storytelling, art, and musicWORKSHOPSHands-on sessions: fermenting, preserving, foraging, baking, and more★"Every event is a collaboration—between people, plants, and ideas."🌿EDIBLE GARDENS &FOOD CONSERVATIONSurrounding LA PIPA are edible gardens designed with permaculture principles: food forests, herbal spirals, pollinator-friendly beds, and seasonal vegetable plots.We grow, harvest, preserve, and compost in cycles that honor the natural flow of abundance.Through food conservation practices—fermenting, drying, curing, and canning—we preserve the memory of each season.We share the knowledge of self-sufficiency that once sustained rural life across Northern Spain.TASTE & LEARNROOTED IN NATURECulinary creativity grows from the soil itself.CREATIVITY ROOTEDIN NATUREOur inspiration comes from the Asturian landscape—from cider apples and wild herbs to mountain cheeses and coastal salt.Food becomes a language through which we explore ecology, design, and emotion. Residencies, collaborations, and public programs bring together chefs, artists, and researchers.FROM THE GARDENFOODGALLERYExplore our culinary projects and special events🌶️SPECIAL EVENTFUEGO Y TIERRAAstur-Mexican culinary experience using our homegrown peppers — from mild Black Olive to legendary Carolina Reaper. A fiery fusion of Asturian gardens and Mexican tradition.EXPLORE THE HEAT →★JOINTHE TABLEWhether you''re a local neighbor, visiting traveler, or part of a global creative community—you''re invited.GET IN TOUCHShare a meal / Learn a craft / Join a gatheringFRIDAY LUNCHES•SECRET DINNERS•WORKSHOPSEVERYONE IS WELCOME','2026-08-05T00:00:00Z') on conflict (document_id,version) do update set content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,byte_count=excluded.byte_count,extracted_text=excluded.extracted_text;
