Capture timestamp: 2026-08-05T01:12:44.427Z

Page description: Astur-Mexican culinary experience at LA PIPA using homegrown peppers from our Asturian garden. Traditional Mexican recipes with Carolina Reaper, Trinidad Scorpion, Habanero, and more.

ClubFoodFuego-y-tierraASTUR-MEXICAN EXPERIENCEFUEGO&TIERRAEl fuego se comparte, pero se respeta.Cocina mexicana y picante desde el huerto asturianoQUIÉNES SOMOSLa PIPA Culinary, led by Dory Casas, is a space where cooking becomes language, the land a laboratory, and spice a shared culture. From Gijón we unite knowledge from north and south to cook without haste, with fire, soul and humor.THE GARDEN AS LABGrowing habaneros, Trinidad Scorpion or Carolina Reaper under the Cantabrian sky is alchemy: each plant is a conversation between climates and cultures. In this experience, the Atlantic becomes spicy and corn is twinned with cider.CHILE CULTUREIn Mexico, chile is identity: history, medicine and culinary poetry. It''s not just spicy: it awakens the body, unites people and balances the plate with lime, corn, avocado and salt. A taco is not a taco without chile, and gathering without fire is just a meeting."The spice is not dominated: it is danced."A little habanero is a mischievous caress; a drop of Reaper, a declaration of love and war.FROM OUR GARDENTHEPEPPERS🫒BLACK OLIVE8,000-15,000 SHUSmoky and elegant with a dark violet-black color. Perfect for pickles, veggie tacos, and rice dishes.SMOKYELEGANT🌶️HABANERO100,000-350,000 SHUFloral, fruity and citric. Orange-red beauty perfect for salsas, marinades, and even chocolate dishes.FRUITYCITRIC🦂TRINIDAD SCORPION1,200,000 SHUIntense yellow with sweet initial flavor then a dry fire punch. For grilled meats and spicy jams.SWEETPOWERFUL💀CAROLINA REAPER1,800,000-2,200,000 SHUThe king of peppers. Fruity, smoky with persistent burn. Use sparingly in infused oils and concentrated salsas.EXTREMELEGENDARYSCOVILLE HEAT SCALEMILD0-10,000MEDIUM10,000-50,000HOT50,000-350,000INFERNAL350,000-2,200,000THERECIPESTraditional Mexican dishes with homegrown Asturian peppersASTURIAN TACOSPork cooked in natural cider with habanero BBQ sauce. The Atlantic meets Mexico.⏱️ Time: 2 hours🌶️ Heat: Medium👥 Serves: 6-8KEY INGREDIENTS• 1kg pork shoulder• 330ml natural cider• 2 tbsp habanero salsa• Smoked paprika• Corn tortillasMANGO HABANERO SALSASweet and smoky with a tropical kick. Perfect balance of fire and fruit.⏱️ Time: 15 minutes🌶️ Heat: Medium👥 Serves: 6KEY INGREDIENTS• 2 orange habaneros (seeded)• 1 ripe mango• Juice of 2 limes• Honey or agave• Extra virgin olive oil🌽ESQUITESGarden corn with habanero butter and cotija cheese🫘BLACK BEAN DIPCreamy with Carolina Reaper infused oil🍫REAPER TRUFFLESDark chocolate with a dangerous twistTHEBARTequila, Mezcal & Cocktails to balance the heat🍹GREEN MARGARITAHabanero, cucumber & lime. Refreshing fire.TEQUILA BLANCO • TRIPLE SEC • LIME • CUCUMBER • HABANERO🍊SPICY PALOMAGrapefruit with chile salt rim. Classic with heat.TEQUILA • GRAPEFRUIT • SODA • CHILE SALT🍎ASTURIAN FUSIONCider meets mezcal. North & South in a glass.DRY ASTURIAN CIDER • MEZCAL • LIMETEQUILA SELECTIONBLANCOS• Don Julio Blanco• Cazadores Blanco• Casa DragonesREPOSADOS• Herradura Reposado• Clase Azul• Ocho ReposadoMEZCALES• Del Maguey Vida• Montelobos Espadín• Los AmantesLA PIPAEXPERIENCE PLAYLISTTHE FIREDOESN''T SEPARATEIT UNITESCook without haste; serve with joy.If you don''t cry a little, maybe you need one more drop of salsa.← BACK TO FOOD','2026-08-05T00:00:00Z') on conflict (document_id,version) do update set content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,byte_count=excluded.byte_count,extracted_text=excluded.extracted_text;
