Page description: LA PIPA''s commitment to protecting your privacy. Learn how we collect, use, and safeguard your personal data in compliance with GDPR.

Privacy PolicyYour privacy is not just a policy—it''s a principle.Last updated: January 2025At LA PIPA, we believe in Privacy by Design and Privacy by Default. This policy explains how we collect, use, protect, and respect your personal data in accordance with GDPR, ePrivacy Directive, and UK Data Protection Act 2018.Data ControllerLA PIPA IS LA PIPAGijón, Asturias, Spainprivacy@lapipa.io1. What Data We CollectInformation You ProvideName and email address (contact forms, newsletter)Messages and inquiries you send usAccount information (if you create an account)Automatically Collected DataCookie consent preferences and timestampsAnonymized IP addresses (hashed for privacy)Browser type and device informationPage visits and navigation patterns (with consent)Session IDs for security and functionality2. How We Use Your DataEssential OperationsRespond to your inquiries and messagesProvide services you''ve requestedMaintain security and prevent fraudComply with legal obligationsWith Your ConsentSend newsletters and updates (opt-in only)Analyze site usage to improve experiencePersonalize content and recommendationsMarketing and promotional activities3. Legal Basis for ProcessingUnder GDPR, we process your personal data based on:Consent: When you explicitly agree (e.g., cookie banner, newsletter signup)Legitimate Interest: For essential site functionality and securityContractual Necessity: To provide services you''ve requestedLegal Obligation: To comply with applicable laws4. Data Sharing & Third PartiesWe minimize data sharing. When necessary, we only share with:Analytics Services (With Consent)Google Analytics 4, Google Tag Manager - for understanding site usage and improving experience. Data is anonymized and stored in EU/US servers.Infrastructure ProvidersSupabase (database, EU region), Vercel (hosting) - for secure data storage and site delivery.Email ServicesResend.com - for transactional emails only (contact form responses, notifications).We never sell your data. All third-party processors are GDPR-compliant and bound by data protection agreements.5. Your Privacy RightsUnder GDPR and UK Data Protection Act, you have the following rights:Right to AccessRequest a copy of your personal data we holdRight to ErasureRequest deletion of your personal data (''right to be forgotten'')Right to RectificationCorrect inaccurate or incomplete dataRight to PortabilityReceive your data in a structured, machine-readable formatRight to ObjectObject to processing based on legitimate interestsRight to Withdraw ConsentWithdraw consent at any time (e.g., via cookie preferences)To exercise any of these rights, contact us at privacy@lapipa.io. We will respond within 30 days as required by GDPR.6. Data SecurityWe implement industry-standard security measures:Encrypted data transmission (TLS/SSL)Secure database storage in EU region (Supabase)Row-Level Security (RLS) policiesIP address hashing for anonymizationRegular security audits and updatesAccess controls and authentication7. Data RetentionWe retain personal data only as long as necessary for the purposes outlined in this policy:Consent logs: 3 years (for GDPR compliance documentation)Contact inquiries: 2 years or until resolvedAnalytics data: 26 months (Google Analytics default)Account data: Until account deletion or inactivity period8. International Data TransfersYour data is primarily stored in the EU (Supabase EU region). When data is transferred outside the EU (e.g., Google Analytics in US), we ensure adequate protection through:Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs)Data Protection Addendums with processorsCompliance with EU-US Data Privacy Framework9. Children''s PrivacyOur services are not directed to individuals under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If you believe we have collected data from a child, contact us immediately at privacy@lapipa.io.10. Changes to This PolicyWe may update this privacy policy to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. We will notify you of significant changes by:Updating the "Last Updated" date at the topDisplaying a notice on our websiteSending an email (if you''re subscribed)Questions or Concerns?We''re committed to transparency and protecting your rights. If you have questions about this policy or how we handle your data, please reach out:privacy@lapipa.ioYou also have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority if you believe your privacy rights have been violated.','2026-08-05T00:00:00Z') on conflict (document_id,version) do update set content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,byte_count=excluded.byte_count,extracted_text=excluded.extracted_text;
