insert into kb.document_versions (document_id,version,content_sha256,mime_type,byte_count,extracted_text,effective_from) values ((select id from kb.documents where document_id='LP-WEB-LIVE-STUDIO-HACKSPACE-DOC'),'2026-08-05-capture','d6b40fad7b9c403b5c0dded47ab04543a7494cb12b1a67a9dddcd18f8b10bcb8','text/markdown',5449,'Archive source LP-WEB-LIVE-STUDIO-HACKSPACE. Hackspace - Open Source Tech Lab — LA PIPA.

Captured public page: https://www.lapipa.io/studio/hackspace

Capture timestamp: 2026-08-05T01:11:54.031Z

Page description: Cyberpunk maker lab in rural Asturias. Experimenting with AI, robotics, TinyGo, computer vision, and open-source hardware. Where code meets countryside.

StudioHackspace[ SYSTEM ACTIVE ]HACKSPACEHACKSPACEOPEN SOURCE × AI × ROBOTICS × INNOVATIONTinyGoGoLangGobotGoCVComputer VisionAIR&D[ PROTOCOL ]OPEN SOURCEMANIFESTO[01]HACK_EVERYTHINGBreak systems apart. Understand how they work. Rebuild them better. Open source means transparent, auditable, improvable code.[02]BUILD_FUTUREFrom TinyGo microcontrollers to computer vision systems, we prototype the technology that doesn''t exist yet.[03]SHARE_KNOWLEDGEEvery project documented. Every failure a lesson. Every breakthrough shared with the global maker community.""The question isn''t whether machines think — it''s whether we still do.— RON EVANS[ VISIONARY THINKING ]Ron Evans'' 2019 VisionRon Evans'' groundbreaking vision from LA PIPA Hackspace in 2019 about data, machine learning, and the real world. Six years later in 2025, his predictions have proven remarkably prescient. Working alongside Alex Lawton, they saw the future clearly—and that future is now our present reality. What a vision.[ FEATURED INTERVIEW ]Channel 9 Microsoft TVRon Evans × Alex Lawton // hosted by Aaron Wislang[ COMMUNITY ]Go Developers Network (GDN)Ron Evans at LA PIPA Hackspace program with The Go Developers Network, bringing together people who code in Go from meetup groups organized all over the planet.[ TECHNOLOGY STACK ]THE_LABGoLang_Ecosystem→TinyGoMicrocontroller programming→GobotRobotics & IoT framework→GoCVComputer vision in GoAI_Systems→Machine LearningNeural networks & models→Computer VisionImage processing & analysis→Edge AIOn-device intelligenceRobotics_Lab→DronesAutonomous flight systems→Embedded SystemsMicrocontroller projects→Sensors & ActuatorsPhysical computingR&D_Projects→ExperimentationRapid prototyping→InnovationPushing boundaries→Open SourceCommunity-driven developmentGO TIME LIVE! #gotimefmRON EVANSLOOKING BACKAT GO FROM2053How did Go survive the thirty years between today and the future perspective shared by Ron Evans (deadprogram), Mat Ryer, and Natalie Pistunovich? What changed about the language to keep it relevant for all these years?ABOUT THE EPISODEStreamed live on 14 June 2022, this special Go Time episode features LA PIPA Hackspace community member Ron Evans (deadprogram) alongside Mat Ryer and Natalie Pistunovich in a fascinating thought experiment about the future of the Go programming language.The conversation explores how Go evolved over thirty years, what changes kept it relevant, and the innovations that shaped programming from a 2053 perspective.Chat with the community in the #gotimefm channel of Gophers SlackMORE FROM RON EVANSRon also appeared on the Changelog podcast discussing open source hardware, robotics, and the maker movement that drives communities like LA PIPA Hackspace.WATCH THE FULL EPISODEFEATURING• Ron Evans (deadprogram)• Mat Ryer• Natalie Pistunovich⚡PROTOTYPEITERATESHAREWe don''t believe in keeping knowledge locked up. Everything we learn, every failure, every breakthrough—we document and share with the community.Open source isn''t just a licensing model. It''s a commitment to collective growth, transparency, and the belief that great ideas deserve to spread freely.FREE & OPENLIVE TECH SHOW#DEADPROGRAMSEASON 01Live open-source technology show conducted by Ron Evans at LA PIPA Hackspace in Asturias, northern Spain. Watch all 10 episodes of Season 1 where we explore hardware hacking, robotics, and maker culture in real-time.EPISODE 01S1_01_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:59:00EPISODE 02S1_02_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:55:22EPISODE 03S1_03_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:59:48EPISODE 04S1_04_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:58:34EPISODE 05S1_05_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:55:22EPISODE 06S1_06_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:58:38EPISODE 07S1_07_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:58:42EPISODE 08S1_08_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:58:34EPISODE 09S1_09_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:59:54EPISODE 10S1_10_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPADuration: 01:49:2310 EPISODES • 19+ HOURS OF LIVE HACKINGLIVE TECH SHOW // SEASON TWO#DEADPROGRAMSEASON 02Produced by Alex Lawton and led by Ron Evans live at LA PIPA Hackspace in Asturias. Season 2 continues the journey of open-source hardware hacking, robotics, and maker culture.EPISODE 01S2_01_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 1EPISODE 02S2_02_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 2EPISODE 03S2_03_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 3EPISODE 04S2_04_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 4EPISODE 05S2_05_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 5EPISODE 06S2_06_DEADPROGRAM@LA PIPASeason 2 Episode 6SEASON 02 // MORE EPISODES COMING⚡JOINTHE LABWhether you''re an experienced maker or just getting started, our hackspace welcomes everyone who''s curious and ready to create.GET INVOLVEDOpen nights / Workshops / Build sessionsLEARN•MAKE•SHAREOPEN SOURCE × OPEN MINDS[ ORIGIN STORY // 2019 ]The essence of Open SourceRon Evans at LA PIPA on one of the Hackspace''s first days in 2019[ GET INVOLVED ]Join the LabInterested in collaborating, learning, or contributing to our open source projects? Let''s connect.SEND MESSAGE','2026-08-05T00:00:00Z') on conflict (document_id,version) do update set content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,byte_count=excluded.byte_count,extracted_text=excluded.extracted_text;
