The Negative Impact of Silos on consumer Marketing structures: Re: Thinking Client and Media Agency frameworks

[ { "type": "highlight", "id": "90a00dad-d0c6-4033-be24-2953785cd933", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" }, { "type": "highlight", "id": "2350ae6e-a21a-4223-ad1e-e752119a7b6f", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" }, { "type": "highlight", "id": "36eded9e-75d5-422e-8f06-58dd6454584f", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" }, { "type": "highlight", "id": "c5760edf-05d9-406d-9f94-e6970c695ba1", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" }, { "type": "highlight", "id": "2aba8808-5796-4f78-bd57-a6f54925b6bf", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" }, { "type": "highlight", "id": "98da339d-7dce-444f-9d5d-9d73df66bada", "shape": "underline", "isFront": false, "isAnimationEnabled": false, "animation": "draw", "duration": 0.5, "direction": "right", "color": { "type": "THEME_COLOR" }, "thickness": { "unit": "em", "value": 0.1 }, "linecap": "square" } ] The age of digitalization has brought about a myriad of specialized channels and platforms to add to the (often underrated) pre-existing marketing mix. From social media to content marketing, search engine optimization to programmatic buying, every aspect of marketing today seems to necessitate its own unique strategy. While specialization can ensure depth of understanding, easier recruitment, talent replacement, and process optimization in the short term the increasing number of silos in marketing —distinct units that operate independently from others— has always raised my concerns.Here I will try to share some of the negative repercussions of these silos on both the client side and within media agencies that I have experienced over the years:Fragmented StrategyClient Side: Brands seeking a cohesive marketing strategy are finding it challenging when each silo operates with its own objectives and tactics. This can result in mixed messaging to consumers and missed opportunities for cross-channel synergy.Media Agencies: Media agencies, in their bid to offer specialized services, may overlook integrated strategies.',876,'214a5303178e9eb9a18dafd80374f956b951eb07f57ddb39db0ea8e2035efd4a','en','historically_published_capture','public',true,'{"chunk_profile":"LP-RAG-CHUNK-1.0","max_characters":3600,"overlap_characters":400,"token_count_method":"ceil_utf16_characters_divided_by_4"}'::jsonb) on conflict (chunk_id) do update set content=excluded.content,token_count=excluded.token_count,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,verification_status=excluded.verification_status,access_scope=excluded.access_scope,active=true,metadata=excluded.metadata,updated_at=now();
