Page description: Learn about how LA PIPA uses cookies and similar technologies. Manage your cookie preferences and understand your choices. Cookie PolicyTransparency in every byte. Control in every click.Manage Cookie PreferencesLast updated: January 2025This Cookie Policy explains how LA PIPA uses cookies and similar technologies on lapipa.io. We believe in giving you full control over your data and your browsing experience.What Are Cookies?Cookies are small text files stored on your device (computer, tablet, smartphone) when you visit a website. They help websites remember your preferences, improve functionality, and understand how you use the site.Types of Cookies We UseSession Cookies: Temporary cookies that expire when you close your browserPersistent Cookies: Remain on your device for a set period or until deletedFirst-Party Cookies: Set by lapipa.io directlyThird-Party Cookies: Set by external services (only with your consent)Our Cookie CategoriesWe organize cookies into four categories, giving you granular control over each:Strictly NecessaryAlways ActiveEssential for the website to function properly. Cannot be disabled as they are required for core functionality.What We Use:lapipa_session_idSession management and securityDuration: Session | Type: First-partylapipa_consent_v1Stores your cookie consent preferencesDuration: 12 months | Type: First-partyPreferencesRemember your choices and settings to personalize your experience (language, theme, layout).What We Use:lapipa_themeRemembers your light/dark mode preferenceDuration: 12 months | Type: First-partylapipa_localeStores your language preference (EN/ES)Duration: 12 months | Type: First-partyAnalyticsHelp us understand how visitors use our site so we can improve your experience. All data is anonymized and aggregated.What We Use:Google Analytics 4 (_ga, _ga_*, _gid)Tracks page views, user interactions, and site performance. IP addresses are anonymized.Duration: Up to 2 years | Type: Third-partyGoogle Privacy Policy →Marketing & PersonalizationEnable personalized content, track marketing campaigns, and provide social media features.What We Use:Google Tag ManagerManages and deploys marketing tags and pixels based on your consent preferences.Duration: Varies by tag | Type: Third-partyManaging Your Cookie PreferencesYou have complete control over which cookies we use. You can manage your preferences at any time:Via Our Preference CenterUse our cookie preference center to enable or disable specific categories.Open PreferencesVia Your BrowserMost browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings:• Chrome• Firefox• Safari• EdgeNote: Disabling certain cookies may affect site functionality and your user experience. Strictly necessary cookies cannot be disabled as they are required for core functionality.Changes to This PolicyWe may update this Cookie Policy to reflect changes in technology, legal requirements, or our practices. Check the "Last Updated" date at the top. Significant changes will be communicated via our website banner or email (if subscribed).Questions About Cookies?If you have questions about how we use cookies or want to exercise your privacy rights, please contact us:privacy@lapipa.ioFor more information about your data rights, see our Privacy Policy.',866,'9ba30902be4f0d3a08430efd792818f8e1056577789ac040bfb7cefebcd2e957','en','captured_public_claim','public',true,'{"chunk_profile":"LP-RAG-CHUNK-1.0","max_characters":3600,"overlap_characters":400,"token_count_method":"ceil_utf16_characters_divided_by_4"}'::jsonb) on conflict (chunk_id) do update set content=excluded.content,token_count=excluded.token_count,content_sha256=excluded.content_sha256,verification_status=excluded.verification_status,access_scope=excluded.access_scope,active=true,metadata=excluded.metadata,updated_at=now();
